<Base title="About Base Impact" description="Base Impact Inc. — a Florida nonprofit corporation helping neighbors get connected and small nonprofits keep their technology working in Brevard County.">
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-body mb-4">About Base Impact</h1>
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      Base Impact Inc. is a Florida nonprofit corporation based in Scottsmoor, Brevard County.
      We help neighbors get connected — devices, internet, and the skills to use them — and we help
      small local nonprofits keep their technology working.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Mission</h2>
    <p class="text-body font-medium">
      To help neighbors get connected and help small local nonprofits keep their technology working,
      so that everyone in Brevard County can access the resources they need.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Vision</h2>
    <p>
      A community where every neighbor has a working device, reliable internet, and the skills to
      use them — and where every small nonprofit has the technology support it needs to serve its
      community effectively.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Values</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Access for all</strong> — Technology is not a luxury. Everyone deserves to be connected.</li>
      <li><strong>Local first</strong> — We serve Brevard County because that's where we live. Local problems need local solutions.</li>
      <li><strong>Simple is better</strong> — We make things easier to find and use. Complexity is the enemy of access.</li>
      <li><strong>Immediate needs first</strong> — We start with what's urgent and build from there.</li>
      <li><strong>Community partnership</strong> — We work alongside existing organizations, not in competition with them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">What we do</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Technology access</strong> — Helping neighbors get working devices and internet service.</li>
      <li><strong>Digital skills training</strong> — Walk-throughs for housing portals, job applications, benefits, and online safety.</li>
      <li><strong>Nonprofit tech support</strong> — Free setup, security, and support for churches, pantries, and 1–5 person community groups.</li>
      <li><strong>Resource directory</strong> — A simpler, local starting point that works alongside 211 for finding food, shelter, health, housing, and recovery services.</li>
      <li><strong>Laptop &amp; device training</strong> — Hands-on training with loaned/donated devices for people new to technology.</li>
      <li><strong>AI &amp; technology infrastructure</strong> — Building local AI capability for form filling, document understanding, and tech troubleshooting. No cloud dependency.</li>
      <li><strong>Cell phone &amp; tablet partnerships</strong> — Partnering with cell providers to get free/low-cost phones and tablets to homeless and people in need.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Community involvement</h2>
    <p>Base Impact's founder is deeply rooted in the Brevard County community through years of hands-on volunteer work:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Food service</strong> — Serving meals at local churches and community organizations including LifePointe Ministries' CREW 29 outreach (Thursday dinners) and First United Methodist Church's Community Breakfast.</li>
      <li><strong>Homeless support</strong> — Helping provide showers, clothing, essentials, and toiletries to people experiencing homelessness at LifePointe Ministries.</li>
      <li><strong>Cold-night shelter</strong> — Providing security and support at LifePointe's inclement-weather cold-night shelter, the only one between Titusville and Port Orange.</li>
      <li><strong>Safe shelter</strong> — Helping provide a safe space for people to shelter from weather at community breakfast programs.</li>
      <li><strong>Clothing distribution</strong> — Helping distribute clothing to families and individuals in need.</li>
      <li><strong>Cold-night shelter security</strong> — Providing security and support at cold-night shelters during extreme weather.</li>
      <li><strong>Communications &amp; safety team</strong> — Serving on safety and communications teams at local organizations and events.</li>
      <li><strong>Technology support</strong> — Providing free tech help, device setup, and digital skills training to neighbors and small nonprofits.</li>
      <li><strong>Senior assistance</strong> — Helping elderly community members with transportation, technology, and daily needs.</li>
      <li><strong>Housing connections</strong> — Connecting people experiencing homelessness with housing resources and services.</li>
      <li><strong>Emergency response</strong> — Acquiring and distributing cold weather clothing and supplies to financially strained and low-income elderly residents.</li>
      <li><strong>Community cleanup</strong> — Participating in neighborhood cleanup and beautification efforts.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">This hands-on community experience shapes Base Impact's programs and ensures we understand the real needs of the people we serve.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Organizations where I volunteer</h2>
    <p>Base Impact's founder has volunteered and provided hands-on service at the following verified tax-exempt organizations in Brevard County. These are not formal partnerships — they are places where I have served and built relationships:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>LifePointe Ministries, Inc.</strong> (EIN 45-1198607) — Operates the Titusville Civic Center. Provides homeless showers, clothing, essentials, toiletries, and Thursday evening dinners. Operates the only inclement-weather cold-night shelter between Titusville and Port Orange. Runs CREW 29 outreach ministry. (Fiscal sponsorship pending.)</li>
      <li><strong>No One Hungry, Inc.</strong> (EIN 83-2834992) — Pine St Food Pantry. Food and basic necessities. Homebound senior delivery. Homeless outreach.</li>
      <li><strong>Hope for North Brevard, Inc.</strong> (EIN 27-0352718) — Sponsors Under The Bridge Ministries. Community support and outreach.</li>
      <li><strong>The Rock Church</strong> (EIN 85-2661919) — Mims/Scottsmoor congregation. Worship, community events, outreach to families.</li>
      <li><strong>Under The Bridge Ministries</strong> — Faith-based outreach to homeless. Monday nights under A. Max Brewer Bridge. Sponsored by Hope for North Brevard.</li>
      <li><strong>First Christian Church of Titusville</strong> — Titusville congregation. Worship, fellowship, practical outreach to families.</li>
      <li><strong>First United Methodist Church of Titusville</strong> — Community breakfast program. Food, essentials, clothing distribution, and safe shelter from weather. Partners with LifePointe Ministries for cold-night shelter overflow.</li>
      <li><strong>Brevard Homeless Coalition (CoC)</strong> — Member organization. <a href="https://brevardhomelesscoalition.org/coc/" class="text-accent underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Continuum of Care for Brevard County</a>. Coordinates housing and services for people experiencing homelessness.</li>
      <li><strong>Feed Hope Now</strong> — Upcoming volunteer. Account setup in progress. Food distribution and community support. <a href="https://feedhopenow.org/get-involved/volunteer/" class="text-accent underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">feedhopenow.org</a></li>
    </ul>


    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Transparency &amp; accountability</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Financial transparency</strong> — All financial records available upon request. Annual reports published on this website.</li>
      <li><strong>Conflict of interest policy</strong> — Written policy governing board decisions and potential conflicts.</li>
      <li><strong>Bylaws</strong> — Adopted governing documents available upon request.</li>
      <li><strong>Public support</strong> — Base Impact is supported by individual donations, community partnerships, and grant funding.</li>
      <li><strong>Open communication</strong> — Donors and community members can reach us at info@baseimpact.org.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Volunteer opportunities</h2>
    <p>Base Impact relies on community volunteers. Current opportunities include:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Tech mentors</strong> — Help neighbors learn digital skills one-on-one.</li>
      <li><strong>Device refurbishers</strong> — Clean, repair, and set up donated devices.</li>
      <li><strong>Event helpers</strong> — Assist at community events, resource fairs, and training sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>Outreach volunteers</strong> — Join food service, clothing distribution, and shelter support.</li>
      <li><strong>Grant writers</strong> — Help research and write grant applications.</li>
      <li><strong>Web &amp; tech support</strong> — Help maintain the website and technology systems.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">No experience required — we provide training. Contact us at info@baseimpact.org to get involved.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Infrastructure goals</h2>
    <p>We are seeking grants and partnerships to build our technology infrastructure:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>AI-capable hardware</strong> — Laptops and workstations to run local AI models for privacy-first assistance.</li>
      <li><strong>Training devices</strong> — Laptops and tablets for hands-on digital skills training.</li>
      <li><strong>Cell phone partnerships</strong> — Free/low-cost phones and tablets with data plans for homeless and people in need.</li>
      <li><strong>Device refurbishment</strong> — Program to extend the life of donated technology.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Board of directors</h2>
    <p>Base Impact Inc. is governed by a Board of Directors with three unrelated members, as required for nonprofit governance:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>President</strong> — Oversees mission, strategy, and partnerships.</li>
      <li><strong>Secretary</strong> — Manages records, minutes, and compliance documentation.</li>
      <li><strong>Treasurer</strong> — Oversees financial stewardship, budgeting, and reporting.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint">Board members serve without compensation. Conflicts of interest are managed through a written Conflict of Interest Policy.</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-body mt-6">Fiscal sponsorship</h2>
    <p>Base Impact Inc. is seeking fiscal sponsorship from <strong>LifePointe Ministries, Inc.</strong> (EIN 45-1198607), a verified 501(c)(3) organization. A fiscal sponsorship agreement is in progress but not yet finalized. Once approved, this partnership will allow Base Impact to receive tax-deductible donations and operate programs while its own 501(c)(3) application is pending.</p>

